        "created_at": "2014-12-22T19:27:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>How do we know it's really Witcher?</p><p>To conduct a test, we need to prepare a very large scale and find out if it weighs the same as a duck. Since ducks float in water, we can deduct that Witcher should also be able to be bouyant and most likely made out of wood, and can be successfully ignited. Thus, the Witcher test will be successfully concluded after proving the Witcher can burn.</p><p>The contest will be to determine who can perform this very scientifically proven method the fastest.</p>",
